e via system last-input time; logs an Idle record after IdleThresholdSec (default 300 s)\\n  - CSV output with header: timestamp,state,title,process_name,process_id\\n  - Default log file: <script folder>/active-window-log.csv\\n\\nNotes\\n- This script uses Win32 APIs (user32.dll) and must run on Windows PowerShell or PowerShell 7 on Windows.\\n\\nHow to run\\n- Open PowerShell (Windows PowerShell or pwsh on Windows):\\n  - Example (default settings):\\n    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\\\path\\\\to\\\\track.ps1\"\\n  - Example (custom settings):\\n    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\\\path\\\\to\\\\track.ps1\" -IntervalMs 500 -IdleThresholdSec 120 -LogFile \"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\active-window-log.csv\"\\n- View the log live:\\n  Get-Content \"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\active-window-log.csv\" -Wait\\n\\nRun in background\\n- PowerShell background job:\\n  Start-Job -ScriptBlock { & \"C:\\\\path\\\\to\\\\track.ps1\" -IntervalMs 1000 -IdleThresholdSec 300 -LogFile \"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\active-window-log.csv\" }\\n- Or as a scheduled task for auto-start at logon (high-level):\\n  - Use Task Scheduler > Create Task > Trigger: At log on\\n  - Action: Start a program\\n  - Program/script: powershell.exe (or pwsh.exe)\\n  - Arguments: -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\\\path\\\\to\\\\track.ps1\" -IntervalMs 1000 -IdleThresholdSec 300 -LogFile \"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\active-window-log.csv\"\\n\\nStopping the script\\n- Press Ctrl+C in the session running the script, or stop the background job/scheduled task.\\n\\nIf you want me to adjust the idle timeout, log format, or add app categorization (e.g., mapping process names to project tags), let me know.', task_completed='true', outputs={}, thought='', action='finish')], inputs={}, outputs={}, agent_state=<AgentState.FINISHED: 'finished'>, resume_state=None, traffic_control_state=<TrafficControlState.NORMAL: 'normal'>, metrics=Metrics({'accumulated_cost': 0.13760675, 'costs': [{'model': 'openai/gpt-5'